		<p><span class="newheads">Other Resources:</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>(Listed by Release Date)</strong></p>
		<ul>



<li><a href="/surveys/international/">2024, International Activities Program (IAP): This page provides a compilation of indicators from a multitude of data sources with a rich array of information on the current state of education internationally.</a><br /></li>

<li><a href="/surveys/pisa/">2024, Program for International Student Assessment (PISA): This site provides access to publications and data that focus on 15-year-olds' capabilities in reading literacy, mathematics literacy, and science literacy.</a><br /></li>

<li><a href="/surveys/pirls/">2024, Progress in International Reading Literacy Study (PIRLS): This site features publications and data on the comparative study of the reading literacy of 4th grade students.</a><br /></li>

<li><a href="/timss">2024, Trends in International Mathematics and Science Study (TIMSS): This site provides access to publications and data on the mathematics and science achievement of U.S. 4th- and 8th-grade students.</a><br /></li>

<li><a href="/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2023115">2023, Highlights of PISA 2022 U.S. Results: This web report provides key comparative information on the reading, mathematics, and science literacy performance of 15-year-old students in the United States.</a><br /></li>

<li><a href="/transfer.asp?sec=true&location=www.oecd.org/education/education-at-a-glance/">2023, Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development, Education at a Glance 2023: This report contains information from the OECD on the state of education around the world.</a><br /></li>

<li><a href="/surveys/pirls/pirls2021/index.asp">2023, PIRLS 2021 U.S. Highlights: Explore selected findings from U.S. participation in PIRLS 2021.</a><br /></li>

<li><a href="/blogs/nces/post/new-international-data-show-large-and-widening-gaps-between-high-and-low-performing-u-s-4th-and-8th-graders-in-mathematics-and-science">2021, NCES Blog, New International Data Show Large and Widening Gaps Between High- and Low-Performing U.S. 4th- and 8th-Graders in Mathematics and Science</a><br /></li>

<li><a href="/timss/results19/index.asp#/math/intlcompare">2021, TIMSS 2019 U.S. Results: Explore how U.S. 4th- and 8th-grade students' mathematics and science performance compared internationally in 2019.</a><br /></li>

<li><a href="https://nces.ed.gov/blogs/nces/post/new-data-from-the-trends-in-international-mathematics-and-science-study">2017, NCES Blog, New Data From the Trends in International Mathematics and Science Study</a><br /></li>

<li><a href="http://nces.ed.gov/pubsearch/pubsinfo.asp?pubid=2016100">2015, Comparative Indicators of Education in the United States and Other G-20 Countries: 2015</a><br /></li>
</ul>

